/** @mainpage Qore v8 Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section v8intro v8 Module Introduction

    The \c v8 module allows for the execution and management of JavaScript code in %Qore.

    To use the module in a %Qore script, use the \c %%requires directive as follows:
    @code{.py} %requires v8 @endcode

    Note that while JavaScript and v8 support threading, calls into a single
    @ref V8::JavaScriptProgram "JavaScriptProgram" are subject to thread serialization; only one thread can be active

    Also included with the \c v8 module:
    - @ref typescriptactioninterfaceintro "TypeScriptActionInterface" an API for
      allowing data provider app actions to be created from TypeScript / JavaScript

    Main classes:
    - @ref V8::JavaScriptProgram "JavaScriptProgram"
    - @ref V8::TypeScriptProgram "TypeScriptProgram"
    - @ref V8::JavaScriptObject "JavaScriptObject"

    @section v8sandboxing Sandboxing

    JavaScript and TypeScript code run by this module has file, process and network access through Node.js, which no
    %Qore sandbox sees or controls.  The classes of the module are therefore uncontrolled APIs (functional domains
    \c EMBEDDED_LOGIC and \c UNCONTROLLED_API): code that a sandbox governs can neither create a program nor run
    JavaScript code through an object of the module unless the sandbox allows uncontrolled APIs
    (\c SandboxManager::setUncontrolledApiPolicy()), and gets \c INVALID-FUNCTION-ACCESS.  This also holds when
    trusted code that the sandboxed code calls creates the program for it, unless the trusted code does so under a
    system-policy barrier (\c SandboxManager::createSystemPolicyCall()).  A host must never allow uncontrolled APIs to
    code that it does not trust, as such code can then reach anything in the process.

    @section v8qlibmodules Qore User Modules

    - @ref typescriptactioninterfaceintro "TypeScriptActionInterface" — an API for Qore DataProvider app actions in TypeScript
    - @ref typescriptproxyintro "TypeScriptProxy" — definitions for a TypeScript proxy API

